# Ignore everything...
*
# ...but still descend into folders to look for content
!*/
# ...and keep markdown files
!*.md
# ...and images, so note embeds work
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
!*.gif
!*.webp
!*.svg
# ...and canvases and base dashboards
!*.canvas
!*.base
# ...and this file itself
!.gitignore
# ...and .gitattributes, which the `*` rule above would otherwise swallow
!.gitattributes

# Unlike public_vault, .obsidian IS tracked here. The point of this vault is to
# be a starting point you can clone and open, so the setup ships with it:
# the enabled plugins, the Templater config and its folder template.
!*.json
!*.js
!*.css

# ...except the view state, which Obsidian rewrites just from looking at a
# pane. Same reason .base and .canvas are untracked in master_vault.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Dropbox sync artifacts
*conflicted copy*
